# Benchmark results and reports
/results/
# `/reports/*` rather than `/reports/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so excluding the directory would make the negation below a
# silent no-op.
/reports/*
/discopt_benchmarks/reports/
# ...except the Phase 0 Regime-N baselines. These are not run output, they are the
# frozen REFERENCE every Regime-N card is gated against (consolidation plan §0.1):
# `panel_baseline.py --check reports/panel_baseline_<sha>.json` is meaningless if
# the baseline is not in the repository at the sha it names.
!/reports/panel_baseline_*.json
# ...and the Phase 5 coverage census, for the same reason: it is the ranking that
# ORDERS the Phase-5 sub-cards (plan Phase 5.1), so a later card must be able to
# read the table it is sequenced against rather than re-derive it.
!/reports/phase5_kernel_coverage_census_*.json
# ...and the Phase 5.4 differential panel, which is the Regime-C evidence for the
# DISCOPT_CONVEX_KERNEL graduation decision recorded in the plan's §6.
!/reports/phase5_convex_kernel_diff_panel_*.json
!/reports/phase5_convex_kernel_budget_entry_*.json
# ...and the Card 3a(b) entry-experiment artifacts, which are the whole deliverable
# of that card: it landed ZERO production edits, so its §6 verdicts ("both stay",
# with the disagreement counts) are only auditable if the measurements they cite
# are in the repository.
!/reports/card3a_*.json
!/reports/card3a_*.log
# ...and the Card 4c H-RHS entry experiment, cited by the §6 entry that justifies
# refusing a non-zero `Constraint.rhs` (66 models, 3,705 executed comparisons).
!/reports/card4c_rhs_entry.log
# ...and the open-ledger item 15 root-cause artifacts. They are the evidence that
# the Regime-N panel's flakiness is the solver's wall-clock-bounded root heuristic
# rather than the harness, which is what justifies hardening the gate by
# replicate-and-agree instead of narrowing the `comparable` population.
!/reports/item15_*.json
!/reports/item15_*.log

